# COMMON ERRORS AND SOLUTIONS

## ERROR 1: Port 8080 Already in Use

Incorrect command:

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8080:80 nginx
```

Reason: Port 8080 is already occupied, possibly by Jenkins.

Correct command:

```bash
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

Open:

http://localhost:8082

## ERROR 2: Container Name Already in Use

Error:

```text
Conflict. The container name "/nginxdemo" is already in use.
```

Solution:

```bash
docker ps -a
docker rm -f nginxdemo
docker run -d --name nginxdemo -p 8082:80 nginx
```

## ERROR 3: Docker Hub DNS Error

Error:

```text
lookup registry-1.docker.io: no such host
```

Check internet:

```bash
ping google.com
```

Check DNS:

```bash
nslookup registry-1.docker.io
```

Test Docker Hub:

```bash
docker pull hello-world
```

Restart Docker Desktop if required and resolve network/DNS issues.

Pull Nagios again:

```bash
docker pull jasonrivers/nagios:latest
```

## ERROR 4: Pod ImagePullBackOff

Check:

```bash
kubectl get pods
kubectl describe pod POD_NAME
```

Solution: Verify image name, image tag and internet connectivity.

## ERROR 5: HPA Shows Unknown CPU

Check:

```bash
minikube addons enable metrics-server
kubectl get pods -n kube-system
kubectl get hpa
kubectl top pods
```

Verify that CPU resource requests are configured.

## ERROR 6: Nagios Configuration Error

Check:

```bash
docker exec -it nagiosdemo bash
/opt/nagios/bin/nagios -v /opt/nagios/etc/nagios.cfg
```

Correct configuration errors before restarting Nagios.

